## ADR 0020 lines naming a run subject's shape
27:  - a run's subject is the base, the one patch and the input files its records name;
30:  A Result keeps **one subject per cited run**, `{base, patch, files}`, instead of one merged `fingerprints` list. A Hypothesis is covered when one entry holds its whole subject, so a run at B plus a patch never covers bare B. An old Result reads as one entry with no base. The word `fingerprints` stays for the hashed files inside a subject (Q-D906CD).
